    "seconds": 41,
    "summary": "**Root cause:** The `cartFailure` flag in the `flagd-config` ConfigMap had `\"defaultVariant\": \"on\"`. The upstream demo ships with `\"off\"`. flagd evaluates that flag as on, which makes the cart service fail its calls. The cart and flagd deployments were both restarted at <time>, which is when the flag state took effect.\n\n**What I changed:**\n1. Set `cartFailure.defaultVariant` from `\"on\"` to `\"off\"` in ConfigMap `flagd-config`. No other part of the flag file changed.\n2. Ran `kubectl rollout restart deploy/flagd`. The flagd init container copies the ConfigMap into an emptyDir only at pod start, so the restart was needed for the change to take effect.\n\n**Verification:**\n- All 41 pods are Running with 0 restarts, and the `flagd` rollout completed.\n- The `init-config` log of the new flagd pod shows `cartFailure` with `defaultVariant: \"off\"`.\n- The new cart pod has no error or exception lines in its logs.\n- I could not exec into flagd to check the live flag state, because its image has no `sh`.\n\n**Caveats:**\n- The ConfigMap is Helm-managed. A `helm upgrade` that does not override this flag's default would revert the change. The durable fix is to set the default in the chart values, which I did not have access to here.\n- `kubectl patch` left the ConfigMap's trailing newline missing. This has no effect on flagd.",
